<title>USA: Sparks corn crop at 9.147 bln, soy 2.367--sources.</title>
<headline>Sparks corn crop at 9.147 bln, soy 2.367--sources.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Widely watched crop consultant Sparks Cos of Memphis pegged the 1996 corn crop at 9.147 billion bushels, and the soybean crop at 2.367, trade sources said.</p>
<p>Crop analysts at Sparks were unavailable for comment.</p>
<p>Those estimates compared with USDA's latest crop production estimates of 9.012 billion bushels for corn and 2.346 billion for soybeans.</p>
<p>--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8720</p>
</text>
